      "definition": "Reconstitute a function, structure, identity, or system after hidden, compacted, exhausted, or no-longer-viable material has been exposed and can no longer remain unchanged.",
      "functionalAim": "Restore viability, depth, integrity, and concentrated agency through exposure, elimination, redistribution, and reorganization of what has become toxic, compulsive, concealed, or structurally unsustainable."
    },
    "coreQuestions": [
      "What can no longer continue in its current form?",
      "What hidden material is organizing this system?",
      "What must be exposed before regeneration is possible?",
      "Which resource, attachment, or power pattern must be redistributed?",
      "What remains viable after the nonviable material is removed?"
    ],
